From 1b108946c421d80a348c0f9aac7bd1c30df69f1b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:06:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 14/46] lowering: the discarded-result flag describes only the
 top-level inc/dec

Salvaged from the pre-#857 swizzle series (8b8696444), where it was found:
the flag stayed set while a post-inc/dec lowered its operand, so in
`(p++)->w++;` the inner p++ also took the discard path, yielded the
incremented pointer, and the increment landed in the next element. The flag
is consumed on entry; the vector inc/dec takes it as a parameter.

Test: postinc_discard_lvalue.c (GCC-compared, -O1).
