From 2ec702d6eb4ac8c15e3e86c1a449cfe9f1c63c22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:39:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 15/46] backend: make compile time linear in call sites (new-C)

A function with N calls took O(N^2) in five places; 4000 calls took
168 s at -O0 and 149 s at -O2 (x86-64).  Each fix keeps the exact
semantics of the code it replaces; x86-64 asm is byte-identical on all
2587 corpus files at -O0 and -O2.

- x86 peephole liveness: the call guard scanned a window of lines for
  every call marker; it now checks the exact marker (O(1)).  The second
  dead-value proof is kept and answered from the per-file liveness.
- relay_and_lea: family_private_* scans the family span once.
- copy_coalesce / fortify_fold: one per-function use set instead of a
  rescan for every candidate.
- generation: the remat audit runs in one pass.
- x86 emit: home_sharers keeps an inverse map (S11).
- location_alloc: UseIndex records per-value use points, use/def blocks,
  phi feeds and segments once per plan_function (immutable there), and
  Pressure caches block peaks.  The old scans stay as #[cfg(test)]
  references; assert_use_index_matches_scans checks the index against
  them on 6 fixtures, and a debug_assert rescans the peaks cache.

calls  -O0 before/after       -O2 before/after
1000   10974 ms / 1003 ms     9301 ms / 733 ms
2000   41509 ms / 1938 ms     35947 ms / 1540 ms
4000   167945 ms / 4042 ms    149027 ms / 3093 ms
