From 5295f3576525d228bbb824d00a4e93e0b33088d3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 11:40:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/46] ext_vector_type: Clang 23.1.3 swizzle parity
 (selectors, diagnostics, lowering)

Verified rule by rule against Clang 23.1.3:
- lo/hi/even/odd select (N+1)/2 lanes; bool vectors take no selectors.
- A modified duplicate selection is "vector is not assignable (contains
  duplicate components)"; & of a selection or ext subscript is "address of
  vector element requested" (GNU &gv[i] stays valid).
- Caret columns: illegal component at operator+1+index, "exceeds" at the
  operator.  Mixed sets report the first offending letter ('r' in .xr).
- Multi-lane ext ++/-- is rejected.
- Lowering: nested selections compose onto the root and evaluate it once;
  lanes past the vector length read 0 and absorb stores; an assignment loads
  every source lane before storing (overlap-safe).

tests/regression/ext_vector_select: select.c (runtime vs Clang -O0) and
errors.c (exact line:col diagnostics).
