From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:47:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 18/46] i686 peephole: width-exact narrow zero test; exact
 boolean model in compare-branch fusion

fold_narrow_load_imm_compare rewrote `movzwl M,%r; testl %r,%r` as
`cmpb $0, M` -- one byte of a word, so 0x0100 tested as zero -- and spelled
the register-source form `cmpb $0, %ax` (re-encoded by assemblers as
`cmpb $0, %al`).  Every truthiness test of an `unsigned short` with a zero
low byte took the wrong branch at -O0/-O1/-O2.  The zero test now matches
the load width: `cmp{b,w} $0, M` for memory, `test{b,w} %r, %r` for a
register (same flags as `cmp $0`, and the shape later fusions match).

fuse_compare_and_branch pattern-skipped any `LoadEbp`, any `movsbl/movswl`
and accepted `testl %eax,%eax` straight after `setCC %al`, then deleted
everything from the setCC through the test -- stores included.  That
branched on an unrelated reload, read bits 8..31 that setCC never wrote,
erased published stores, and deleted a boolean the fallthrough still read
(`switch ((x < 0) + 0)` returned garbage via a function pointer).  The scan
now models where the boolean lives (%al; all of %eax only after an
extension; dword slots written from %eax and reloaded whole), always drops
the redundant re-test (every admitted line preserves EFLAGS), and removes
the setCC and extensions only when no store published the boolean and
GprLiveness proves %eax dead after the jump.  This is the contract the
x86-64 pass already enforces (b_extensionless_wide_test_refuses,
b_foreign_stack_reload_of_the_carrier_refuses,
b_live_carrier_after_the_jump_refuses).

Tests: unit fixtures now carry function context (liveness needs it) and
assert the sound contract; new refusal/acceptance/width tests; regression
i686_word_zero_test{,_o0}.c and i686_fused_branch_live_boolean.c fail on
the parent and pass here.
