Subject: [PATCH 20/46] i686: fused compare+select; 32-bit-pattern compare
 immediates

i686 never implemented supports_fused_cmp_select, so every compare feeding
a select materialised `setCC; movzbl` and re-tested it before
`jne .Lsel_true`; the peephole could drop the re-test but not the boolean
without a liveness proof it usually cannot get (a void function's `ret`
looks like an %eax reader).  emit_fused_cmp_select_impl emits the compare
with the same direct/staged flag emitters and load->memory fold as the
fused branch, then `jCC .Lsel_true` and the shared select arms.  Generation
only fuses an adjacent single-use integer compare (never float/long
double/128-bit or 32-bit-target I64), and adjacency keeps the %ecx staging
inside the scratch-hazard model (see the doc comment).

Compare emitters now take an I64 constant in [i32::MIN, u32::MAX] (e.g.
0x80000000 against a U32) as the same 32-bit immediate the old
`movl $v,%ecx` staging meant, instead of a dead %ecx load.

Coverage: i686_cmp_select_matrix.c (every predicate x width x signedness x
operand shape x int/long long/double arms, hashed, compared with GCC);
artifacts/pr833/csel_stress.py ran the unrolled 64152-check variant at
-O0/-O1/-O2: PASS.
