From 0895f07c97424cb1c7a6a6fb15c8f21c12347b1c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 12:51:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/46] tests: ext-vector self-checks agree with Clang 23.1.3
 and fail on every bit

ext_vector_swizzle.c and ext_vector_long_double_layout.c returned their
failure mask from main; an exit status keeps 8 bits, so checks 8..25
(swizzle) and 9..15 (layout) could never fail the run -- the swizzle test
printed "FAIL (0x10000)" and passed.  Both now `return bad != 0`.

With every bit visible, three swizzle checks turned out to assert
non-Clang semantics (Clang 23.1.3 rejects or disagrees):
* `m.s1`, `m.s07`, `m.lo` on a `_Bool` ext vector: "illegal vector
  component name" -- bool vectors take subscripts only (pinned by
  ext_vector_select/errors.c).  The packed-bool checks use subscripts and
  now also verify the untouched neighbour lanes.
* `t.hi.y` on a 3-lane vector: odd N is laid out as N+1 lanes, so `hi` is
  lanes {2, 3} and `.y` is the padding lane (unspecified; never written
  for `tc`).  The checks read lane 2 as `hi.x`, the lane they meant (same
  expected values).

Both files: clang-23.1.3 -O0 (m64, m32) and lccc -O0/-O2/-m32 -O0/-m32 -O2
print ok and exit 0.
---
 .../ext_vector_long_double_layout.c           |  2 +-
 tests/regression/ext_vector_swizzle.c         | 20 +++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 13 insertions(+), 9 deletions(-)

