From 54b510f11a03920fcd9880f9baf7ab9ac2b444ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lccc-agent <agent@arena.invalid>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 15:40:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/46] compile time: remove quadratic/cubic terms from
 mem2reg, phi elim, call splitting, GPR load hoisting

A function made of a long sequence of loop nests (1152 in a generated
stress main) compiled in 121 s at -m32 -O0 (GCC: 24 s for the whole TU).
Callgrind self-cost growth per doubling identified the terms; every fix
below is output-preserving (assembly byte-identical at 144/288/576 nests,
corpus 1028/0/5 under CCC_VALIDATE_SSA=1):

* phi_eliminate::fold_computed_phi_incomings: the dominated-region
  profitability sweep visited every block with an idom-chain walk per
  candidate copy -- O(copies x blocks x depth).  It now consults a
  value -> touching-blocks index (built once; the fold only moves
  instructions within their block) with O(1) Euler-interval dominance.
* DominanceChecker moves from passes::loop_analysis to ir::analysis (the
  layer both depend on; loop_analysis re-exports it).
* split_call_spanning_ranges: phi-dest / phi-incoming / use-count facts
  came from a whole-function scan per live interval; one pass now.  A
  declined split no longer re-solves liveness: candidates are ranked once
  (stable, uses descending -- the same sequence the repeated arg-max
  produced) and walked until one applies.  The site scan uses one reverse
  last-use scan per block.  Ids for a wrap are checked before mutating, so
  id exhaustion can no longer leave an inserted alloca unsynced.
* hoist_loop_invariant_gpr_load: per back-edge it scanned the whole file
  for the header label and the whole function twice for its CFI bounds.
  A label map and a CfiIndex (binary search over .cfi markers, shifted on
  the pass's single insert_line) replace the scans; loop_entry_is_unique
  takes the range instead of rescanning.
* mem2reg rename: iterative dominator-tree walk with an undo log (pop
  exactly this block's definitions) and a phi-dest -> alloca map, instead
  of recursion that snapshotted every alloca's stack depth per block.  A
  50 000-deep dominator chain overflowed a 1 MiB stack before (unit test
  proves: SIGABRT on the old code); now it runs in heap.

576 nests, -O0: 32.2 s -> 9.6 s.

Tests: relay_and_lea::cfi_index_matches_function_range_scan (index vs scan
on every line, nopped marker, open function, inserts);
promote::rename_walk_handles_deep_dominator_chain.
