Subject: [PATCH 31/46] x86 FMA: in-place 231-form for slot-resident
 multiplicands; 132-form stages a slot addend

emit_scalar_fma231_with only formed `acc + a*b` in the destination's XMM
home when the multiply LHS was register-homed. A slot-resident factor sent
the whole FMA through the 4-instruction scratch path (acc->xmm0, lhs->xmm1,
fma, xmm0->dest). fma_mul_sources now picks the sources for every shape:
both homed (direct), one homed (swap -- IEEE multiplication is exactly
commutative, so the fused result is bit-identical; the other factor rides
as the memory operand), neither homed (lhs staged in the sanctioned %xmm1
scratch, rhs as memory, or %xmm1 again for x*x). A factor homed at the
destination still goes to the 132-form, which now also stages a
slot-resident addend in %xmm0 like a constant addend. Homes are read
through fresh_home_of, the clobber guard path 2b already used.

Callgrind -O2 (x86-64-v3 default), 31 fast benchmarks vs the parent:
struct_copy 218122778 -> 188122778 Ir (-13.75%), the other 30 identical in
every counter. -O2 -mavx -mfma A/B over 282 FP corpus/benchmark programs:
280 identical stdout+rc, 2 differ (the new tests, fixed). The regression
test is self-checking with exact products; mutation-checked (forcing %xmm1
as src2 -> bad=16; dropping the %xmm0 addend load -> bad=32).
