Subject: [PATCH 44/46] frontend: C scoping of enumerators/tags, VM
 typeof/sizeof, ICE/NPC, static refs (S77)

Ordinary-identifier namespace (C11 6.2.1, 6.2.3):
- Enumerators resolve by scope in sema (enumerator_refs keyed by ExprId) and
  lowering consumes that resolution (identifier_enumerator) instead of a
  name-based enum map; replaces #868's depth comparison. Fixes wrong code in
  both shadowing directions, incl. a local shadowing a LATER file-scope
  enumerator (reduced from binutils 2.47 tc-i386.c i386_generate_nops, where
  `offsetT disp` was narrowed to int at -O0).
- Tags/enumerators declared inside type names register per statement; a
  selection/iteration statement and each substatement is a block (C11
  6.8.4p3, 6.8.5p5) in both sema and lowering (type-only scopes, no frames).

Variably modified types:
- vm_layout.rs: one VM layout query for typeof/sizeof/__auto_type; pointers
  to VLAs carry pointee strides (inc/dec, compound +/-, subscripts).
- __auto_type decays arrays/functions at all three sites.

Constant expressions: a single ICE checker (sema/ice.rs) and NPC predicate;
GNU constant builtins; conditional-operator pointer result types.

Static functions: reference collection over all AST contexts (walkers), and
dead_statics runs at every level (also -O0/-O1): unreferenced statics that
call undefined functions no longer reach the link.

Tests (outputs identical to gcc-16 -O0/-O2/-m32 and clang 23.1.3):
enum_ordinary_namespace_lowering.c, vla_vm_type_layout.c,
static_function_refs_vm_contexts.c, conditional_pointer_types.c,
gnu_constant_builtins.c; check_sema_constraints.sh block.
