Dual-layout selection emits a reordered function twice more and runs the
full peephole over both candidates. At -O0 it buys nothing: on four
binutils 2.47 TUs (gas expr.c, read.c, tc-i386.c; bfd elflink.c) the
exploration-free output has identical instruction counts and equal or
smaller .text, while compile time drops 35-40% (Callgrind, expr.c -O0:
18.996G -> 11.460G Ir). -O1 and up keep it (0.2-0.6% smaller .text).
relayout_blocks_static_chain takes an explicit DualLayout policy; unit test
chain_only_reorders_identically_without_a_record pins the contract.
