From 8c2347f9cfdc7581c35b7692d85227d1339f8afd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ms178-arena <arena@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:09:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 46/46] C23 frontend: constexpr objects, fixed enum types,
 sema-owned static asserts, char identity

constexpr (C23 6.7.1p5-6, 6.6p7):
- Parser records object-level restrict/_Atomic per declarator (the specifier
  _Atomic is the pointee's: `_Atomic int *p` vs `int *_Atomic p`, which now
  parses), constexpr ordering versus _Thread_local/auto, and rejects storage
  classes on parameters ("storage class specified for parameter 'x'"), which
  previously leaked onto the enclosing declaration.
- sema/analysis/constexpr.rs: declaration rules (typedef/extern/_Thread_local/
  auto, underspecified tags, single declarator, initialized data, invalid
  qualifiers) and initializer rules over a shared C11 6.7.9 initializer walk
  (sema/init_cursor.rs, unit-tested): ICE for integers, exact
  representability (incl. bit-fields, long double -> double via binary128),
  null pointers; members (incl. implicit zeros, union active member) become
  named constants usable in ICEs and static initializers.
- Static assertions are decided by sema only (GCC 16.2 rules and wording:
  "not an integer" / "not constant" / "failed"); enumerators and constexpr
  objects are the only named values.

Pre-existing miscompiles fixed on the way:
- `const double d = -1u;` folded to -1.0 (unsigned sources were read signed);
  folding now goes through one fold_to_type with source-type reads, single
  rounding, and exact long double values (FoldedValue::LongDouble).
- Qualifiers after the base type (`char const c`, `double const d`) were
  dropped.
- Lowering's packed-enum width rule truncated >32-bit packed enums to 4 bytes
  while sema used 8; both now use EnumType.

C23 enums with fixed underlying type (6.7.2.2): parse (bit-field
disambiguation), type/size/ABI, enumerator types, range/overflow and
redeclaration diagnostics, forward `enum E : T;`. Enum value evaluation is
single-sourced (type_builder::enum_type_of); the redundant re-evaluation in
sema's tag registration is removed.

Plus the earlier S80 work: plain/signed/unsigned char identity (string
literals were typed signed under -funsigned-char), CType::NullPtr, unified
_Generic matcher, C23 preprocessor/lexer additions, operand constraints.

Oracle evidence (gcc-16 -std=c23, locations stripped): constexpr table
87/89 MATCH as last measured (the auto-order case was fixed afterwards, unmeasured;
remaining: GCC folds `&g != 0`); fixed-enum diagnostics 16/16;
s80_cx.c and s80_enum_fixed.c runtime output identical to GCC 16.2 and
Clang 23.1.3 at -O0/-O2.
